      "type": "custom-section-float-tip",
      "blocks": {
        "tip_KWhAcG": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "lightning_bolt",
            "title": "Significantly Reduce Stress: ",
            "text": "<p>Scientific studies have shown that floating can lower cortisol levels—the body’s primary stress hormone. By lowering cortisol, you and your partner can experience a deep sense of calm, improving your relationship and overall well-being.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tip_diK7d7": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "title": "Enhance Connection and Communication",
            "text": "<p>In a world full of noise, a float session creates a rare opportunity for silent, shared introspection. This peaceful environment can encourage openness and understanding, helping you feel more connected to your partner.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tip_P4GGdn": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "snowflake",
            "title": "Improve Sleep Quality",
            "text": "<p>Our tanks are packed with magnesium-rich Epsom salt. As you float, your body absorbs this key mineral, often called the “relaxation mineral,” which is known to aid sleep and calm the nervous system.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tip_eEiiGa": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "face",
            "title": "Support Physical Health:",
            "text": "<p>The zero-gravity environment of the float tank takes pressure off your joints and muscles, improving blood flow and reducing chronic pain. It’s a fantastic way to recover after a long day or intense workout.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tip_pJPNTz": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "swim",
            "custom_icon": "shopify://shop_images/benefits-icon-_7.png",
            "title": "Boost Creativity and Mental Clarity:",
            "text": "<p>By removing external sensory input, floating allows your brain to enter a restorative “Theta state.” This is the same brainwave state associated with deep meditation, creativity, and new problem-solving.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tip_CyF6cD": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "title": "Strengthen Your Bond:",
            "text": "<p>Doing something new and profound together—especially something that requires you to be present and surrender to the experience—can be incredibly bonding.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
